  "context": [
    "The Urban Cruiser Hyryder, launched in 2022, was Toyota's first India-specific SUV built jointly with Maruti Suzuki (which sells the same platform as the Grand Vitara), and it introduced Toyota's self-charging strong-hybrid system to the mainstream mid-size SUV segment at a price point well below imported hybrids.",
    "The hybrid variant pairs a 1.5-litre petrol engine with an electric motor and e-CVT, needs no external charging, and delivers real-world efficiency gains that resale buyers specifically seek out, which is why hybrid Hyryders consistently command a resale premium over the plain-petrol and CNG versions at the same age and mileage.",
    "Toyota's decades-long reputation for reliability and low running costs in India, combined with the hybrid's fuel-saving pitch, gives the Hyryder one of the flattest depreciation curves in the midsize SUV segment, clearly ahead of segment peers like the Hyundai Creta or Kia Seltos at the same age.",
    "The optional all-wheel-drive AllGrip variant, offered on the petrol rather than the hybrid, adds a modest resale premium for buyers in hill-station and semi-rural markets, though it remains a small share of overall Hyryder transactions compared to the front-wheel-drive hybrid and petrol variants."
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What is the resale value of a Toyota Hyryder in India?",
      "a": "A Toyota Hyryder retains roughly 78% of its ex-showroom price after two years and about 70% after three years, still around 58% at year five, among the strongest curves in the midsize SUV segment as of September 2026. A 2023 Hybrid V with 10,000-25,000 km currently trades around ₹14-15 lakh."
    },
    {
      "q": "Does the Hyryder Hybrid hold value better than the petrol or CNG version?",
      "a": "Yes, the strong-hybrid variant consistently commands a resale premium of several percentage points over the equivalent plain-petrol Hyryder, reflecting buyers' willingness to pay for its proven fuel-efficiency advantage and Toyota's hybrid reliability record."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why does the Hyryder depreciate slower than a Hyundai Creta or Kia Seltos?",
      "a": "The Hyryder's 3-year retention of about 70% sits roughly 8 points above the Midsize SUV segment average of 62%, driven by Toyota's reliability reputation and the resale demand premium that hybrid powertrains command in India's hybrid-starved SUV market."
    },
    {
      "q": "How much does a Hyryder depreciate per year?",
      "a": "A Hyryder loses about 13% of value in year one, with 4-6 percentage point annual retention drops through year five (to roughly 58%), noticeably flatter than the midsize SUV segment average of 49% at the same age."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which city gives the best resale price for a Hyryder?",
      "a": "Bengaluru trades around +3% above the national mid, driven by the highest hybrid adoption among metros and ride-hailing uptake, while Kolkata trades roughly -2% due to slower SUV turnover there."
    }
  ],
